  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal by reason of its layout, siting and incompatible materials is considered to be an insensitive addition which would be visually at odd with the high aesthetic value of the Conservation Area. This would lead to an incongruous, cramped and contrive form of overdevelopment of the plot which would be harmful to the significance of the local heritage asset, the historic built form, the setting and integrity of the host and adjoining buildings, and the character and appearance of the wider Conservation Area. The proposed advertisement is therefore contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF, 2019), policies 7.4, 7.5, 7.6 and 7.8 of the London Plan (2016), DMD 11, DMD 37, DMD 38, DMD 39 and DMD 44 of the Development Management Document (2014) and CP30 and CP31 of the Core Strategy (2010).\r\r",
    "The proposal due to the failure to include sufficient information on acoustic/noise assessment and adequate mitigation for extraction systems necessary to assess feasibility, practicality and adequacy of the proposed plant equipment, in order to make the preliminary amenity assessment, would cause noticeable harm to residential amenity. This is especially so, given the proximity to adjoining residential dwellings to the north, including their private amenity space. As such, the proposal would not comply with the aims and objectives of National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF, 2019), Policies 3.9, 7.2, 7.4 and 7.15 of the London Plan (2016), DMD 32, DMD 34, DMD 64 and DMD 68 of the Development Management Document (2014), as well as CP30 and CP32 of the Core Strategy (2010)."
  ],
